SUMMARY:Out to Lunch: Faith\, Charity & Volunteerism on the Homefront
DESCRIPTION:Connecting to our new exhibit\, “Fighting for our Nation” and using the lens of the Civil War\, this talk will look at Elmira’s contributions to the war efforts. Included will be military recruiting\, participation and civilian support activities happening during that time. \nBring your own lunch and drop by to hear a short talk on local history. Light refreshments provided.These programs are free and open to the public. Call 607-734-4167 for more information
URL:https://chemungvalleymuseum.org/event/out-to-lunch-faith-charity-volunteerism-on-the-homefront/
LOCATION:Chemung Valley Museum\, 415 E. Water Street\, Elmira\, NY\, 14901
CATEGORIES:Talks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://chemungvalleymuseum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/OTL-Faith-Charity.--e1782750995988.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Chemung County Historical Society":MAILTO:cchs@chemungvalleymuseum.org
END:VEVENT
